CSS architecture comparison 
CSS Architecture Comparison." Compare three approaches: BEM, 
Utility-First (Tailwind), and Component-Based Styling. BEM uses 
clear naming rules to keep structure organized, which is helpful in 
large projects. Utility-First (like Tailwind) uses small pre-made 
classes for fast styling, but needs good organization to stay clean. 
Component-Based Styling keeps each component (like a button or 
card) with its own style rules, making code modular and easy to 
maintain. In short, choose BEM for clarity, Utility-First for speed, and 
Component-Based Styling for modular organization